= Model selection bias — Technical =

== Extremal selection ==
Let validation estimates be:

<pre>
C_i = μ_i + ε_i
</pre>

for candidates i.

Selecting:

<pre>
i* = argmin_i C_i
</pre>

creates dependence between i* and the noise ε_i.

Even if individual C_i are approximately unbiased for μ_i, the selected minimum can be optimistically biased.

== Adaptive search ==
Sequential hyperparameter tuning, architecture search, feature engineering, and leaderboard feedback create adaptive dependence that can exceed simple fixed-k multiple comparison.

== Nested estimation ==
Nested cross-validation uses an inner selection loop and outer evaluation loop to estimate the performance of the full model-selection procedure.

